cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Boring Log Viewer"
abstract: >-
  The Boring Log Viewer is open-source software that draws geotechnical boring
  logs from structured data. It reads a boring described in a JSON format,
  defined by a published JSON Schema, and produces a consistent boring log
  drawing: a header, depth and elevation scales, a graphic log with Unified Soil
  Classification System (USCS) symbols and symbols for fill, pavement, organic
  materials and rock, material descriptions, samples and sampler types, blow
  counts, laboratory specimens with their test results, groundwater levels, and
  a legend. A USCS symbol that is not given is inferred from the material
  description only when the description determines it, and recorded symbols are
  checked against their descriptions. Logs can be drawn in three ways: on a web
  page in the browser, with no installation and no data leaving the user's
  computer; through a web service (API) that returns SVG, PNG or HTML for use by
  databases and scripts; and as a JavaScript module in other web pages or
  Node.js programs. Translators convert Excel workbooks laid out like the
  provided template, and AGS4 and DIGGS data-transfer files, into the same JSON
  format. Users can define their own columns, layouts, hatch patterns and
  sampler symbols. The software is used to display boring logs in geotechnical
  case-history databases such as the Next Generation Liquefaction (NGL) database
  and VSPDB.
